  <p>Product loss is a cost that quietly melts away in daily production. Even a small difference in carryover can, on a high-tonnage <a href="/en/industries/pulses/">pulses</a> or nut line, add up by year's end to sums that overshadow machine prices. This line item usually goes unseen in the used-machine calculation — yet that is where the real decision is made.</p>

